/T (Qualifying policy This is a policy which can pay its proceeds, free of tax, if the conditions have been met. Quartile In statistics the quartile point is the spot where one quarter of the items in a series is on one side and three quarters are on the other side. For example, if a series of numbers was 1, 3, #, 4, 5, 7, 10, 20 and 30, the quartile point \(#\) would be between 3 and 4. Quorum A quorum is the lowest number of qualifying people needed for a meeting to be valid.)
