431 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Statutory books By law, companies must keep books of account to show and explain all their transactions. These are called statutory books. Statutory Sick Pay Employers have to pay this to employees who are off work because of sickness. The Government sets Statutory Sick Pay rates. Stockbroker A stockbroker buys and sells stocks and shares for clients. Stock control Stock control is a system for keeping adequate control of stock levels and for preventing stock losses. Stock exchange A stock exchange is a market for stocks and shares. Organisations can raise capital by selling securities through a stock exchange. Stock in trade This is the term for goods bought but which have not yet been sold. Sub judice If something is sub judice, it is being dealt with by the court and cannot be discussed outside the court. Subscribers Subscribers are the people who set up a limited company. Subsidiary A subsidiary is a company controlled by another company. The control is normally a result of having more than 50% of the voting rights. Superannuation This is a regular contribution to a pension scheme by an employee. Surcharge This is an extra charge banks make if a customer does not keep to their agreement with the bank.)
/E (Statutory books By law, companies must keep books of account to show and explain all their transactions. These are called statutory books. Statutory Sick Pay Employers have to pay this to employees who are off work because of sickness. The Government sets Statutory Sick Pay rates. Stockbroker A stockbroker buys and sells stocks and shares for clients. Stock control Stock control is a system for keeping adequate control of stock levels and for preventing stock losses. Stock exchange A stock exchange is a market for stocks and shares. Organisations can raise capital by selling securities through a stock exchange. Stock in trade This is the term for goods bought but which have not yet been sold. Sub judice If something is sub judice, it is being dealt with by the court and cannot be discussed outside the court. Subscribers Subscribers are the people who set up a limited company. Subsidiary A subsidiary is a company controlled by another company. The control is normally a result of having more than 50% of the voting rights. Superannuation This is a regular contribution to a pension scheme by an employee. Surcharge This is an extra charge banks make if a customer does not keep to their agreement with the bank.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [2]
>>
